age, and it must be invoked on the composed production path rather than tested as an isolated helper. Separately the assigned Section 17.3 still has no scoped implementation owner and must be made traceable without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: identity currently attests objects that violate the pinned closed contract, which is an attestation-integrity defect rather than a missing test."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8)\nRework closes CR revision 1 attestation bypass. Production call site prepareObjectIdentity now invokes validateImmutableObjectShape before CalculateObjectIdentity or VerifyObjectIdentity can attest. Exact Blob Descriptor/BlobChunk and recursive Transfer Manifest closed shapes refuse unknown top/nested members and chunk order/bounds/coverage violations; Section 17.3 migrated-from identity contribution is traceable without migration publication or atomic-reference claims. Final standalone gates all exited 0: focused/race/80.7% coverage, three canonical fuzz targets plus scalar fuzz at fixed 100x, scoped tracecheck for 1.6/10.1-10.4/17.3, trace tests, catalog check, full tests/coverage, vet, build, Linux/Windows cross-test builds, diff check, and board validate. Board validate retains 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and does not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-validation-logs.tar.gz.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, pid=53577, exit=0)\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate, so review must confirm the closed-shape validator is on the composed production path for every scoped schema, refuses without over-refusing valid objects, and that section 17.3 traceability is honest."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, pid=14322, exit=0)\nCR revision 2 review returned three blocking findings and they fall into two mirror classes, so the rework must be an AUDIT rather than three spot fixes. F1 under-validates: validateMigrationExtensionObject inspects only works.relux.ax.migrated-