unch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, pid=14322, exit=0)\nCR revision 2 review returned three blocking findings and they fall into two mirror classes, so the rework must be an AUDIT rather than three spot fixes. F1 under-validates: validateMigrationExtensionObject inspects only works.relux.ax.migrated-from, so a Transfer Manifest carrying extensions with the key not_namespaced is attested by both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity. F2 over-validates in the opposite direction: Section 1.6 bounds string[n..m] in UTF-8 CHARACTERS and ManifestEntry.target is string[1..4096], but the validator compares len(target) in bytes, so a valid 3999-character 5999-byte target is refused. Do not fix only the two fields the reviewer named. Sweep closed_shapes.go for every open or extension point and validate its full key grammar, and for every string bound switch to character counting consistent with the common scalar contract. Prove both directions at the production entries. F3 is a gate gap in the suite this candidate itself extended: the closed-shape fuzz target is defined but never invoked, so wire every defined target into the configured suite with a fixed -fuzztime.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965