er-bound classes in both directions, and honest README claims. The Story candidate is story_final and carries the whole Story delta, so the final review sees all three leaves in one candidate; re-checkpointing the earlier leaves is neither required nor intended.\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: restore the accepted leaf content verbatim and complete the systematic scoped-constraint derivation on a freshly provisioned, consistent workspace.\"\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-032aa6, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run RUN-260831-1c6191 cancelled by operator; operator action required; reason: Would fail identically: base refresh replayed the branch but left checkpoint_oid at the pre-replay OID.\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-032aa6)\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-032aa6, pid=40684, exit=0)\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate covering all three leaves after a workspace recovery; review must confirm the previously accepted leaf content is unchanged except where this leaf legitimately extends it, and attack the scoped constraint derivation in both directions.\"\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-baf438, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-baf438)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-baf438, pid=54730, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-baf438 queued successor RUN-260831-273ee2 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-273ee2)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-273ee2, pid=63472, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-273ee2 queued successor RUN-260831-60192c (attempt 2/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-60192c)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-60192c, pid=86097, exit=0)\nFifth review round, and the failure mode is structural rather than substantive. Each round the validator gains cases for exactly the schemas the previous review named, and the next review finds the next uncovered schema. Revision 4 has schema-specific cases only for Blob Descriptor and Transfer Manifest, so every other registered immutable schema including urn:ax:schema:session-record@1.0.0 falls through to extension-only validation and is attested without its Section 10.1 envelope members. Stop enumerating. Make the property total: every schema in the registered self-identity set must resolve to a schema-specific shape validator, and add a completeness test DERIVED FROM THE REGISTRY that fails when any registered schema lacks one. That is the same structural fix that ended the identical cycle on the normative pin task, where a derived union plus a regression assertion replaced a hand-picked list. Where member sets can be read from the pinned specification or the generated contract catalog, derive them rather than transcribing. A schema whose shape genuinely has no additional constraints beyond the envelope still needs an explicit registered validator saying so, not a fall-through."}}]},{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260831-fd3a76365e4533deceb82540","sequence":116,"timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:49:36.996629Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"6d2e8b01-2cc4-4e49-994a-05938b6ce680"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"TASK-260830-8x76g1","element_type":"task"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260831-612f78fcb64a6fef6f411c72","causal_order":1,"operation":"checklist","changes":[{"field":"checklist_item","after":{"kind":"checklist_item","checklist_item":{"Text":"The closed-shape validator is TOTAL over the registered self-identity schema set: every registered schema resolves to a schema-specific shape validator, and a non-circular completeness test derived from the registry fails when any registered schema has no validator, so a newly registered schema cannot silently fall through to extension-only checking","Checked":false}},"checklist_index":27}]},{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260831-74e14d6210180c18d317b6a0","sequence":115,"timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:48:41.735616Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"codex"},"run":{"availabili